      "value": "@{5a4c8e898a8de943b225818b|full_name}: I'd like to think that the deterrent for this scenario would be the same for if a raid group went around forcing vote-kicks. That is: the possibility of having a mod called on the whole raid group would make the raid participants more reluctant to co-operate in irrefutably punishable behavior.\n\nSince an avatar ban is actually less disruptive than a world kick, I can see how it might be seen as being 'safer' for abuse. But since the affected parties would still be around to observe and report their behaviors, this kind of trolling would likely be seen overall as bearing a higher risk for participants.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
