  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2017-12-31T22:25:59.363Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I've seen a lot of comments in the discord about dealing with certain raid-type avatars in VRChat, so I thought I'd open up a Canny to further the discussion.\n\nPersonally, I'm not against raids as they can be a lot of fun if executed correctly, but in some cases a raid is just not wanted in a world. Maybe the world's inhabitants just want to chill, maybe there's another impromptu event already going on, or maybe the raid is just too toxic.\n\nMost raids are united under a single publicly available avatar. Therefore, the simplest solution is to allow world inhabitants to vote-ban the raid avatar if the raid is unwanted.\n\nThe vote would apply to all players in the world who aren't wearing the avatar in question. If the vote passes, all players in the world will see the avatar replaced by an unobtrusive avatar indicating that the avatar has been banned from that world.\n\nThis would be a light-handed solution as the raid party is still given the option to stay (minus their raid apparel), or move on to another world more accepting of their activities.\n\nThis would also be a beneficial solution for dealing with singular instances of disruptive avatars without outright kicking the offending player from the world.\n\nSome notes:\n- Players with a banned avatar are free to switch to another avatar. But if they got their avatar from an avatar world, they will have to return there to get it back. If the player chooses not to change their avatar and instead travels to another world where the ban is not in effect, they will be reverted back to their current avatar.\n- The duration of the avatar ban should be sufficiently long enough to outlast most raid groups.\n- Players with the offending avatar should be excluded from the vote as large raid groups may suddenly comprise the majority for a world.\n- Conversely, it should not be possible to vote-ban an avatar if the vote would pass by default (i.e. the person initiating is the only one without the avatar).\n- It should not be possible to vote-ban an avatar from a world that contains that avatar's pedestal.\n- World creators and other players with moderator-like capabilities should be able to instate an avatar ban without a vote.",
